{#
  view/juser/login/check-email.phtml — the answer to every sign-in request.

  **Every** request, and that is the point of the page rather than a detail of it: an
  unknown address that was just registered, a known one that got a link, a deactivated one
  that got nothing, a throttled one that got nothing, and a mailer that threw all render
  exactly this. Anything added here that reports which of the five happened turns the
  sign-in form into an account oracle.

  So there is no `email` in the copy either, even though the controller passes it — the
  .phtml does not print it, and printing it would be the first step towards a page that
  knows something.
#}
{% extends juser_layout %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate('Check your email') }}</h1>

<p>{{ translate('If that address is valid, we sent you a sign-in link. It expires in %s minutes.')|format(expiration_minutes) }}</p>

<p class="help-block">{{ translate('Nothing in your inbox after a minute or two? Check the spam folder.') }}</p>

<p><a href="{{ juser_path('zfcuser/login') }}">{{ translate('Use a different address') }}</a></p>
{% endblock %}
